L294: ## Impact Statement
L295: 
L296: This paper presents work aimed at advancing the field of Machine Learning, specifically in the domain of streaming and on-device Reinforcement Learning (RL). We believe our contributions have several societal implications worth highlighting.
L297: First, the shift towards on-device learning offers significant privacy advantages. By processing transitions sequentially and discarding them immediately, our approach minimizes data retention and eliminates the need to transmit raw observations to remote servers.
L298: Second, regarding energy consumption, our focus on lightweight, memory-efficient algorithms (avoiding large batches and extensive memory storage) aligns with the goal of reducing carbon emissions. By reducing the computational and memory footprint required for effective RL, we facilitate deployment on low-power edge devices.
